      "message": "Can we use the new java switch syntax with bracket ?\n```suggestion\n                        case \"CLOSED\" -\u003e {\n                            switch (mCurrentState) {\n                                case \"DISPLAY_OFF\" -\u003e Log.d(TAG, \"No action for state \" + nextState);\n                                default -\u003e handleSuspend(false);\n                            }\n                        }\n                        case \"DISPLAY_OFF\" -\u003e {\n                            switch (mCurrentState) {\n                                case \"TABLET\" -\u003e handleSuspend(false);\n                                case \"DOCKED\", \"LAPTOP\" -\u003e handleSuspend(true);\n                                default -\u003e Log.d(TAG, \"No action for state \" + nextState);\n                            }\n                         }\n                        case \"LAPTOP\", \"DOCKED\", \"TABLET\" -\u003e {\n                            switch (mCurrentState) {\n                                case \"CLOSED\", \"DISPLAY_OFF\" -\u003e handleResume();\n                                default -\u003e Log.d(TAG, \"No action for state \" + nextState);\n                            }\n                        }\n                        default -\u003e {\n                            Log.e(TAG, \"Unknown state transition to \" + nextState);\n                            return;\n                        }\n```",
